// NOTE: NOT a clean sibling. At HEAD this ALSO leaks (leak=1) — `run(){firsti(nums)}`
// is a UserCall chain HEAD does not promote, AND firsti's `v[0].to_text()` native
// tail delivery. The generic-vs-nongeneric distinction only appears AFTER the
// UserCall slice + NativeCall-monomorph promotion land. OPEN sub-question (enhance
// later): firsti's `v[0].to_text()` is a native tail that 2d SHOULD promote — why
// does it still leak? (indexing + native-arg? or run's UserCall copy?)
fn firsti(v: vector<integer>) -> text { v[0].to_text() }
fn run() -> text { nums: vector<integer> = [10, 20, 30]; firsti(nums) }
fn main() { print(run()); }
